<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion, reduced 3D corallum & Keulegan-Carpenter surge morphogenesis (Caryophyllia (Caryophyllia) quadragenaria & Pocillopora verrucosa (Scleractinia stony corals))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-5> ;
    schema:about "Caryophyllia (Caryophyllia) quadragenaria & Pocillopora verrucosa (Scleractinia stony corals)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Finite-element or accretive growth of the corallum, validated dissepiment/synapticula geometry, a digitised cross-taxa septa table, verified Pass 3 DOIs, or that the 48 model rim septa match the specimen's 40",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D calice insertion with perimeter-threshold triggering 2 pi R_k = N_hex(k) lambda_s, Kunth Rugosa comparison, a phenomenological boundary-layer flux law j(theta) = j0 (1 + beta sqrt(Pe) cos theta + gamma Pe/(1+Pe) cos 2theta) with Pe = 0 symmetry control, a reduced kinematic 3D conical corallum (cylindrical label volume) with stacked insertion fronts, pali, dissepiments and synapticulae ablated at fixed outer geometry, specimen-measured apical angle (side-profile cone fit) and septal thickness (0.80 R duty cycle), Otsu calice area fraction, an oscillatory surge quasi-steady closure with sgn(U) dipole and a renewal law eta(KC) = 1 - exp(-KC/2pi), KC sweep and reef KC estimates",
        "reported_in_source: Chindapol et al. (2013): advection-diffusion limited accretive growth of Pocillopora verrucosa with upstream-polarised growth under unidirectional flow and symmetric, compact growth under bidirectional (surge) flow",
        "reported_in_source: Keulegan & Carpenter (1958): the ratio U_max T / L governing oscillatory-flow forces on bodies; Falter et al. (2005) and Reidenbach et al. (2006): oscillatory flow enhances mass transfer to reef corals relative to unidirectional flow at the same speed",
        "reported_in_source: Kunth (1869): Paleozoic Rugosa serial insertion in four fossular loci, N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4m",
        "reported_in_source: Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848): hexameral cyclic septal insertion N_hex(k) = 6 * 2^(k-1) with decreasing radial reach of successive cycles",
        "reported_in_source: Wells (1956) Treatise Part F: solitary corallum shape classes by apical angle (ceratoid, trochoid, turbinate, patellate) and the endothecal elements dissepiments and synapticulae",
        "transfer_boundary: The 3D corallum is kinematic (labels assigned from the cone profile), not accretive growth or mechanics; dissepiment/synapticula spacings and thicknesses are modelling choices tagged `provenance: model`",
        "transfer_boundary: The Law 3 flux law and the ellipticity formula are this script's ansatz, not equations from Chindapol et al. (2013); the JSON 'Eqs. (1)-(8)' pointer is unverified",
        "transfer_boundary: The quasi-steady surge closure gives <sqrt(Pe(t))>/sqrt(Pe_max) = 0.763 < 1, i.e. it cannot reproduce the oscillatory mass-transfer ENHANCEMENT of Falter 2005 / Reidenbach 2006; only the symmetry (dipole cancellation) claim of Chindapol 2013 is reproduced" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-04339-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1127/zdgg/21/1869/647>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849>,
