<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion, reduced 3D corallum & Keulegan-Carpenter surge morphogenesis (Caryophyllia (Caryophyllia) quadragenaria & Pocillopora verrucosa (Scleractinia stony corals))",
        "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion, reduced 3D corallum & Keulegan-Carpenter surge morphogenesis faithfully reproduces Caryophyllia (Caryophyllia) quadragenaria & Pocillopora verrucosa (Scleractinia stony corals) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Caryophyllia (Caryophyllia) quadragenaria & Pocillopora verrucosa (Scleractinia stony corals) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-coral-calice-septa-insertion-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py> ;
    schema:about "Caryophyllia (Caryophyllia) quadragenaria & Pocillopora verrucosa (Scleractinia stony corals)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Finite-element or accretive growth of the corallum, validated dissepiment/synapticula geometry, a digitised cross-taxa septa table, verified Pass 3 DOIs, or that the 48 model rim septa match the specimen's 40",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D calice insertion with perimeter-threshold triggering 2 pi R_k = N_hex(k) lambda_s, Kunth Rugosa comparison, a phenomenological boundary-layer flux law j(theta) = j0 (1 + beta sqrt(Pe) cos theta + gamma Pe/(1+Pe) cos 2theta) with Pe = 0 symmetry control, a reduced kinematic 3D conical corallum (cylindrical label volume) with stacked insertion fronts, pali, dissepiments and synapticulae ablated at fixed outer geometry, specimen-measured apical angle (side-profile cone fit) and septal thickness (0.80 R duty cycle), Otsu calice area fraction, an oscillatory surge quasi-steady closure with sgn(U) dipole and a renewal law eta(KC) = 1 - exp(-KC/2pi), KC sweep and reef KC estimates",
        "reported_in_source: Chindapol et al. (2013): advection-diffusion limited accretive growth of Pocillopora verrucosa with upstream-polarised growth under unidirectional flow and symmetric, compact growth under bidirectional (surge) flow",
        "reported_in_source: Keulegan & Carpenter (1958): the ratio U_max T / L governing oscillatory-flow forces on bodies; Falter et al. (2005) and Reidenbach et al. (2006): oscillatory flow enhances mass transfer to reef corals relative to unidirectional flow at the same speed",
        "reported_in_source: Kunth (1869): Paleozoic Rugosa serial insertion in four fossular loci, N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4m",
        "reported_in_source: Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848): hexameral cyclic septal insertion N_hex(k) = 6 * 2^(k-1) with decreasing radial reach of successive cycles",
        "reported_in_source: Wells (1956) Treatise Part F: solitary corallum shape classes by apical angle (ceratoid, trochoid, turbinate, patellate) and the endothecal elements dissepiments and synapticulae",
        "transfer_boundary: The 3D corallum is kinematic (labels assigned from the cone profile), not accretive growth or mechanics; dissepiment/synapticula spacings and thicknesses are modelling choices tagged `provenance: model`",
        "transfer_boundary: The Law 3 flux law and the ellipticity formula are this script's ansatz, not equations from Chindapol et al. (2013); the JSON 'Eqs. (1)-(8)' pointer is unverified",
        "transfer_boundary: The quasi-steady surge closure gives <sqrt(Pe(t))>/sqrt(Pe_max) = 0.763 < 1, i.e. it cannot reproduce the oscillatory mass-transfer ENHANCEMENT of Falter 2005 / Reidenbach 2006; only the symmetry (dipole cancellation) claim of Chindapol 2013 is reproduced" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py; output: docs/media/coral_calice_septa_insertion_comparison.png; organism: Caryophyllia (Caryophyllia) quadragenaria & Pocillopora verrucosa (Scleractinia stony corals); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/e651a8b8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 0cff1aa51273708b6f3a81f44e78a537ce76e9aebe378d1738d5aa43189cae7d; artifact_sha256: cbee31b2b54319f1b348c2f440156314a4a9df33e06b7982c07b3a007457ba13; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json=9984d41d12285bd0..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/corallum3d_surge_reference.json=5d3be9bdd005bfad..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scleractinian_coral_septa_specimen.jpg=904035c936843361..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scout_manifest.json=325761c7cb0d58db...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-coral-calice-septa-insertion-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848): hexameral cyclic septal insertion N_hex(k) = 6 * 2^(k-1) with decreasing radial reach of successive cycles | Kunth (1869): Paleozoic Rugosa serial insertion in four fossular loci, N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4m | Chindapol et al. (2013): advection-diffusion limited accretive growth of Pocillopora verrucosa with upstream-polarised growth under unidirectional flow and symmetric, compact growth under bidirectional (surge) flow | Wells (1956) Treatise Part F: solitary corallum shape classes by apical angle (ceratoid, trochoid, turbinate, patellate) and the endothecal elements dissepiments and synapticulae | Keulegan & Carpenter (1958): the ratio U_max T / L governing oscillatory-flow forces on bodies; Falter et al. (2005) and Reidenbach et al. (2006): oscillatory flow enhances mass transfer to reef corals relative to unidirectional flow at the same speed; reconstructed_in_script: 2D calice insertion with perimeter-threshold triggering 2 pi R_k = N_hex(k) lambda_s, Kunth Rugosa comparison, a phenomenological boundary-layer flux law j(theta) = j0 (1 + beta sqrt(Pe) cos theta + gamma Pe/(1+Pe) cos 2theta) with Pe = 0 symmetry control, a reduced kinematic 3D conical corallum (cylindrical label volume) with stacked insertion fronts, pali, dissepiments and synapticulae ablated at fixed outer geometry, specimen-measured apical angle (side-profile cone fit) and septal thickness (0.80 R duty cycle), Otsu calice area fraction, an oscillatory surge quasi-steady closure with sgn(U) dipole and a renewal law eta(KC) = 1 - exp(-KC/2pi), KC sweep and reef KC estimates; transfer_boundary: The 3D corallum is kinematic (labels assigned from the cone profile), not accretive growth or mechanics; dissepiment/synapticula spacings and thicknesses are modelling choices tagged `provenance: model` | The quasi-steady surge closure gives <sqrt(Pe(t))>/sqrt(Pe_max) = 0.763 < 1, i.e. it cannot reproduce the oscillatory mass-transfer ENHANCEMENT of Falter 2005 / Reidenbach 2006; only the symmetry (dipole cancellation) claim of Chindapol 2013 is reproduced | The Law 3 flux law and the ellipticity formula are this script's ansatz, not equations from Chindapol et al. (2013); the JSON 'Eqs. (1)-(8)' pointer is unverified; does_not_claim: Finite-element or accretive growth of the corallum, validated dissepiment/synapticula geometry, a digitised cross-taxa septa table, verified Pass 3 DOIs, or that the 48 model rim septa match the specimen's 40]; other sources: Scleractinia <https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/bibliography/5663>" ;
