<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion, reduced 3D corallum & Keulegan-Carpenter surge morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Laws 1 and 2 (Milne-Edwards hexameral doubling, Kunth 4-fossula serial insertion) are implemented exactly and machine-checked; the Pass 3 3D corallum correctly stacks the insertion fronts along the growth axis (cycle k present wherever R(z) >= R_k, proven monotone in Lean) and the surge closure correctly reproduces the Chindapol (2013) symmetry statement (dipole cancels under bidirectional flow, bilateral quadrupole survives; proven for mirror phases in Lean). Deductions, two of them new in this round: the Law 3 flux law j0(1 + beta sqrt(Pe) cos theta + gamma Pe/(1+Pe) cos 2theta), the 0.16 j0 wake floor and the ellipticity formula are a phenomenological ansatz, not Chindapol's advection- diffusion equations, and the rim modulation constants 0.035 / 0.025 / 0.42 / 0.35 / 0.06 are unsourced (-5); the 3D corallum is kinematic, not accretive or mechanical, so dissepiments/synapticulae are placed, not grown (-3); the renewal law eta(KC) = 1 - exp(-KC/2pi) is a modelling choice and the quasi-steady closure gives a mean transfer BELOW the unidirectional case (0.763), opposite to the Falter/Reidenbach enhancement (-3). v2's 93 did not price the Law 3 ansatz; v3 does." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py L435–L501: Phenomenological boundary-layer flux law with 0.16 j0 floor clamp (L454) and ellipticity formula (L462): not Chindapol's equations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L435-L501>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion, reduced 3D corallum & Keulegan-Carpenter surge morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "16 reference-anchored measurements now: the 9 Pass 2 entries plus 7 Pass 3 entries, of which four are real external or specimen comparisons (apical angle 36.66 vs Wells trochoid 40 deg; costae 15 vs 20; 3D rim area fraction 0.493 vs specimen Otsu 0.532; KC_50 numeric 4.350 vs analytic 4.355) and two are exact-symmetry checks (3 insertion fronts; <A_1> = 1e-16 vs 0). Deductions, most of them defects v2 did not price: the 7-species r reference 0.9985, the Pe-sweep r reference 0.9990 and the specimen reach-ratio reference 1.4368 are self-referential or hand-set (the reach ratio reference equals the measured value and was copied into the reference JSON), and the new dissepiment volume increment explicitly uses reference = value (-6); the Pe-sweep 'Pearson r vs sqrt(Pe)' correlates a monotone closed form with itself and the Pe = 36 up/down ratio in the script (13.73, floor clamp) still disagrees with the JSON table (14.375) (-4); the cross-taxa `observed_septa_mean` / `typical_peclet_Pe` / `major_minor_reach_ratio` values are recalled, not digitised (-3); the KC_50 check validates the script against its own analytic closed form (-1). quick_gate remains 100." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
