<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) Hexameral Septal Insertion Doubling Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs simultaneous midpoint bifurcation of interseptal chambers in Scleractinian stony corals as the expanding calice perimeter crosses multiples of λ_s | Variables: k ∈ {1..6}: Milne-Edwards insertion cycle order (S1..S6); n_k: newly inserted septa at interseptal midpoints; N_hex(k): cumulative radiating septa; R_k: threshold calice radius; λ_s: inter-septal morphogen wavelength" ;
    dct:source "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) Ann. Sci. Nat. Zool. (Sér. 3) 9:37-89; Cairns & Kitahara (2012) ZooKeys 227:1-47" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L199-L365>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_074_coral_calice_septa_insertion.lean#L21-L58> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def milne_edwards_cumulative_septa : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | k + 1 => 6 * (2 ^ k)
theorem milne_edwards_hexameral_septal_doubling :
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 1 = 6 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 2 = 12 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 3 = 24 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 4 = 48 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 5 = 96 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "n_1 = 6,  n_k = 6 * 2^{k-2} (k >= 2),  N_hex(k) = sum_{j=1}^k n_j = 6 * 2^{k-1} ∈ {6, 12, 24, 48, 96, 192} at 2π R_k = N_hex(k) λ_s" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-04339-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1127/zdgg/21/1869/647>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.227.3612>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2005.50.1.0246>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2006.51.2.1134>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.11574>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.060.043> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Milne-Edwards Hexameral Septal Doubling Law (6 * 2^(k-1)), Kunth's Rugosa Fossula Law (6 + 4m), Chindapol Péclet Advection-Diffusion Calice Symmetry Breaking, Conical Corallum Septal-Front Monotonicity & Keulegan-Carpenter Surge Dipole Cancellation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.milne_edwards_cumulative_septa" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.milne_edwards_hexameral_septal_doubling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kunth's Law (1869) Paleozoic Rugosa Serial 4-Fossula Insertion & Cycle Radial Reach Hierarchy" ;
    dct:description "Contrasts Paleozoic Rugosa serial 4-fossula bilateral insertion against Mesozoic-Recent Scleractinia cyclic hexameral doubling and establishes the decreasing radial reach hierarchy S1 > S2 > S3 > S4 > S5 | Variables: m: Rugosa serial insertion stage across 4 fossulae (2 cardinal, 2 alar); L_k: radial length of cycle-k septa from theca toward central columella; α_k = L_k / R: normalized radial reach" ;
    dct:source "Kunth (1869) Z. Dtsch. Geol. Ges. 21:647-688; Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) Ann. Sci. Nat. Zool. 9:37-89" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L219-L432>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_074_coral_calice_septa_insertion.lean#L64-L105> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def kunth_rugosa_septa (m : Nat) : Nat := 6 + 4 * m
theorem kunth_rugosa_vs_scleractinia_and_reach_hierarchy :
    kunth_rugosa_septa 0 = milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 1 ∧
    kunth_rugosa_septa 3 = 18 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 4 > kunth_rugosa_septa 3 ∧
    septal_cycle_reach_permille 1 > septal_cycle_reach_permille 2 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4 m ∈ {6, 10, 14, 18, 22},   L_k / R = α_k with α_1 > α_2 > α_3 > α_4 > α_5" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-04339-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1127/zdgg/21/1869/647>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.227.3612>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2005.50.1.0246>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2006.51.2.1134>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.11574>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.060.043> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Milne-Edwards Hexameral Septal Doubling Law (6 * 2^(k-1)), Kunth's Rugosa Fossula Law (6 + 4m), Chindapol Péclet Advection-Diffusion Calice Symmetry Breaking, Conical Corallum Septal-Front Monotonicity & Keulegan-Carpenter Surge Dipole Cancellation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.kunth_rugosa_septa" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.kunth_rugosa_vs_scleractinia_and_reach_hierarchy" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Chindapol et al. (2013) Péclet-Modulated Advection-Diffusion Calice Symmetry Breaking Law" ;
    dct:description "Demonstrates exact radial symmetry at Pe = 0 (hydrostatic diffusion limit) and monotonic upstream-enhanced skeletal accretion and calice polarization as Pe increases | Variables: c(x,y): dissolved inorganic carbon / nutrient concentration; Pe = U L / D: Péclet number; s = √Pe: laminar boundary-layer thinning factor; j_n(θ; Pe): normal calcification flux around corallite rim" ;
    dct:source "Chindapol et al. (2013) PLoS Comput. Biol. 9(1):e1002849; Kaandorp & Kübler (2001) Ch. 4-6" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L435-L501>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_074_coral_calice_septa_insertion.lean#L110-L152> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def peclet_flux_dipole_diff (j0 beta s : Int) : Int :=
  peclet_upstream_flux j0 beta s - peclet_downstream_flux j0 beta s
theorem peclet_zero_radial_symmetry (j0 beta : Int) :
    peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta 0 = 0 := by simp [peclet_flux_dipole_diff, peclet_upstream_flux, peclet_downstream_flux]
theorem peclet_advection_upstream_symmetry_breaking :
    peclet_flux_dipole_diff 10 18 0 = 0 ∧
    peclet_flux_dipole_diff 10 18 4 = 1440 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "u · ∇c = D ∇^2 c,  Pe = U L / D,  j_n(θ; Pe) = j_0 (1 + β_Pe √Pe cos θ + γ_Pe (Pe/(1+Pe)) cos 2θ),  Δj = j_up - j_down = 2 j_0 β_Pe √Pe" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-04339-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1127/zdgg/21/1869/647>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.227.3612>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2005.50.1.0246>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2006.51.2.1134>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.11574>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.060.043> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Milne-Edwards Hexameral Septal Doubling Law (6 * 2^(k-1)), Kunth's Rugosa Fossula Law (6 + 4m), Chindapol Péclet Advection-Diffusion Calice Symmetry Breaking, Conical Corallum Septal-Front Monotonicity & Keulegan-Carpenter Surge Dipole Cancellation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.peclet_flux_dipole_diff" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.peclet_advection_upstream_symmetry_breaking" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Pass 3 / Law 4 — Conical (Trochoid/Turbinate) Corallum Septal Insertion Fronts Are Monotone Along the Growth Axis" ;
    dct:description "Extrudes the 2D calice into a reduced 3D cylindrical-voxel corallum resolving septa, dissepiments and synapticulae; proves that the septal insertion fronts are stacked monotonically along z for any cone; apical angle measured from the specimen side profile (36.7° → trochoid) | Variables: z: height along the corallum growth axis; R_ped: pedicel radius; φ: apical angle (Wells 1956 ceratoid 20°, trochoid 40°, turbinate 70°, patellate 120°); k(z): active Milne-Edwards cycle at height z; N(z): septa present at height z; endothecal dissepiments (spacing h_d) and synapticulae (ring radii r_s) fill the loculi between septa" ;
    dct:source "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848); Wells (1956) Treatise Invert. Paleont. Part F pp. F328-F444; Cairns & Kitahara (2012) ZooKeys 227:1-47 glossary" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L630-L930>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_074_coral_calice_septa_insertion.lean#L149-L219> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cone_radius (r_ped slope z : Nat) : Nat := r_ped + slope * z
def active_cycle (r : Nat) : Nat :=
  if r ≥ 800 then 5 else if r ≥ 400 then 4 else if r ≥ 200 then 3 else if r ≥ 100 then 2 else 1
def septa_at_radius (r : Nat) : Nat := milne_edwards_cumulative_septa (active_cycle r)
theorem turbinate_corallum_septal_cycles_monotone :
    (∀ (r_ped slope z₁ z₂ : Nat), z₁ ≤ z₂ →
      septa_at_radius (cone_radius r_ped slope z₁) ≤ septa_at_radius (cone_radius r_ped slope z₂)) ∧
    septa_at_radius (cone_radius 60 1 40) = 12 ∧ septa_at_radius (cone_radius 60 1 340) = 48 := ...
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "R(z) = R_ped + z tan(φ/2) (Wells 1956 classes φ ∈ {20°, 40°, 70°, 120°}),  k(z) = k(R(z)),  N(z) = N_hex(k(R(z))) with z₁ ≤ z₂ ⇒ N(z₁) ≤ N(z₂);  front heights z_k = (R_k − R_ped)/tan(φ/2)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-04339-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1127/zdgg/21/1869/647>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.227.3612>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2005.50.1.0246>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2006.51.2.1134>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.11574>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.060.043> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Milne-Edwards Hexameral Septal Doubling Law (6 * 2^(k-1)), Kunth's Rugosa Fossula Law (6 + 4m), Chindapol Péclet Advection-Diffusion Calice Symmetry Breaking, Conical Corallum Septal-Front Monotonicity & Keulegan-Carpenter Surge Dipole Cancellation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.septa_at_radius" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.turbinate_corallum_septal_cycles_monotone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Pass 3 / Law 5 — Keulegan-Carpenter Oscillatory Surge: Period-Averaged Dipole Cancellation vs Unidirectional Polarization" ;
    dct:description "Couples the Law 3 Péclet flux to bidirectional reef surge: the dipole (upstream polarization) cancels exactly over a period while the quadrupole (bilateral elongation along the surge axis) survives and saturates with KC; contrasts unidirectional current (A₁ = 0.647 at Pe = 16) against surge (⟨A₁⟩ = 0) | Variables: U_max: wave orbital velocity amplitude; T: wave period; L: corallite/colony size; KC: Keulegan-Carpenter number; a = U_max T/(2π): surge excursion; η(KC): boundary-layer renewal efficiency; s = sgn(U)√Pe(t): signed boundary-layer factor; A₁, A₂: period-mean dipole and quadrupole flux asymmetries" ;
    dct:source "Keulegan & Carpenter (1958) J. Res. NBS 60:423-440; Chindapol et al. (2013) PLoS Comput. Biol. 9(1):e1002849 (unidirectional vs bidirectional runs); Falter et al. (2005) & Reidenbach et al. (2006) Limnol. Oceanogr. (oscillatory mass transfer, residual)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L504-L627>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_074_coral_calice_septa_insertion.lean#L221-L248> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem oscillatory_surge_dipole_cancellation (j0 beta s : Int) :
    peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta s + peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta (-s) = 0 ∧
    peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta (-s) = - peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta s := by
  unfold peclet_flux_dipole_diff peclet_upstream_flux peclet_downstream_flux
  constructor <;> simp [Int.mul_neg, Int.mul_add, Int.sub_eq_add_neg] <;> omega
theorem surge_mean_of_mirror_phases_zero (j0 beta s₁ s₂ : Int) :
    peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta s₁ + peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta s₂ +
      peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta (-s₁) + peclet_flux_dipole_diff j0 beta (-s₂) = 0 := ...
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "KC = U_max T / L,  Pe(t) = Pe_max |sin ωt|,  η(KC) = 1 − exp(−KC/2π),  j(θ,t) = j₀[1 + η β √Pe(t) sgn(U) cos θ + η γ (Pe(t)/(1+Pe(t))) cos 2θ],  ⟨Δj⟩_T = 0 (Δj(s) + Δj(−s) = 0),  ⟨A₂⟩(KC) ∝ η(KC) with KC₅₀ = 2π ln 2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-04339-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1127/zdgg/21/1869/647>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.227.3612>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2005.50.1.0246>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2006.51.2.1134>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.11574>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.060.043> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Milne-Edwards Hexameral Septal Doubling Law (6 * 2^(k-1)), Kunth's Rugosa Fossula Law (6 + 4m), Chindapol Péclet Advection-Diffusion Calice Symmetry Breaking, Conical Corallum Septal-Front Monotonicity & Keulegan-Carpenter Surge Dipole Cancellation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.peclet_flux_dipole_diff" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.oscillatory_surge_dipole_cancellation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) Hexameral Septal Insertion Doubling Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs simultaneous midpoint bifurcation of interseptal chambers in Scleractinian stony corals as the expanding calice perimeter crosses multiples of λ_s | Variables: k ∈ {1..6}: Milne-Edwards insertion cycle order (S1..S6); n_k: newly inserted septa at interseptal midpoints; N_hex(k): cumulative radiating septa; R_k: threshold calice radius; λ_s: inter-septal morphogen wavelength" ;
    dct:source "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) Ann. Sci. Nat. Zool. (Sér. 3) 9:37-89; Cairns & Kitahara (2012) ZooKeys 227:1-47" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L199-L365>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_074_coral_calice_septa_insertion.lean#L21-L58> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def milne_edwards_cumulative_septa : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | k + 1 => 6 * (2 ^ k)
theorem milne_edwards_hexameral_septal_doubling :
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 1 = 6 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 2 = 12 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 3 = 24 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 4 = 48 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 5 = 96 := by decide
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "n_1 = 6,  n_k = 6 * 2^{k-2} (k >= 2),  N_hex(k) = sum_{j=1}^k n_j = 6 * 2^{k-1} ∈ {6, 12, 24, 48, 96, 192} at 2π R_k = N_hex(k) λ_s" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-04339-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/TSMC.1979.4310076>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1127/zdgg/21/1869/647>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/zookeys.227.3612>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2005.50.1.0246>,
        <https://doi.org/10.4319/lo.2006.51.2.1134>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.11574>,
        <https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.060.043> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Milne-Edwards Hexameral Septal Doubling Law (6 * 2^(k-1)), Kunth's Rugosa Fossula Law (6 + 4m), Chindapol Péclet Advection-Diffusion Calice Symmetry Breaking, Conical Corallum Septal-Front Monotonicity & Keulegan-Carpenter Surge Dipole Cancellation" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.milne_edwards_cumulative_septa" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_074.milne_edwards_hexameral_septal_doubling" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kunth's Law (1869) Paleozoic Rugosa Serial 4-Fossula Insertion & Cycle Radial Reach Hierarchy" ;
    dct:description "Contrasts Paleozoic Rugosa serial 4-fossula bilateral insertion against Mesozoic-Recent Scleractinia cyclic hexameral doubling and establishes the decreasing radial reach hierarchy S1 > S2 > S3 > S4 > S5 | Variables: m: Rugosa serial insertion stage across 4 fossulae (2 cardinal, 2 alar); L_k: radial length of cycle-k septa from theca toward central columella; α_k = L_k / R: normalized radial reach" ;
    dct:source "Kunth (1869) Z. Dtsch. Geol. Ges. 21:647-688; Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) Ann. Sci. Nat. Zool. 9:37-89" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L219-L432>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_074_coral_calice_septa_insertion.lean#L64-L105> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def kunth_rugosa_septa (m : Nat) : Nat := 6 + 4 * m
theorem kunth_rugosa_vs_scleractinia_and_reach_hierarchy :
    kunth_rugosa_septa 0 = milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 1 ∧
    kunth_rugosa_septa 3 = 18 ∧
    milne_edwards_cumulative_septa 4 > kunth_rugosa_septa 3 ∧
